## DESCRIPTION
##   Working with Vectors
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('Vector', 'Length', 'Tip', 'Tail')
## Tagged by nhamblet

## DBsubject('Calculus')
## DBchapter('Vectors Functions')
## DBsection('Vector Functions and Space Curves')
## Date('1/29/08')
## Author('Darwyn Cook')
## Institution('Alfred University')
## TitleText1('')
## EditionText1('')
## AuthorText1('')
## Section1('')
## Problem1('')
## TitleText2('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## EditionText2('8')
## AuthorText2('Anton')
## Section2('12.5')
## Problem2('3')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',        'PGML.pl',
    'parserVectorUtils.pl', 'contextLimitedVector.pl',
    'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context("Vector");

# the points P and Q
$P = non_zero_point3D();
$Q = non_zero_point3D(0, 10);
while ($P == $Q) { $Q = non_zero_point3D(0, 10) }

$PQ = Vector($Q - $P);

# another 2 points
$X = non_zero_point3D();
while ($X == $P) { $X = non_zero_point3D() }
$Y = non_zero_point3D();
while ($Y == $Q) { $Y = non_zero_point3D() }

#  Main text

$norm = norm($PQ);

Context("LimitedVector-coordinate");

BEGIN_PGML

Consider the vector [`\vec{v}`] from [`P=[$P]`] to [`Q=[$Q]`]. 

a) The vector [`\vec{v}`] is [_]{$PQ}

b) The length of [`\vec{v}`] is [_]{$norm}

c) If the tail of [`\vec{v}`] is at [`[$X]`], then the tip is at [_]{Point($X+$PQ)}

d) If the tip of [`\vec{v}`] is at [`[$Y]`] then its tail is at [_]{Point($Y-$PQ)}

e) What vector has the same length as [`\vec{v}`], but points in the opposite
direction? [_]{-$PQ}

f) What vector has the same direction as [`\vec{v}`], but is twice as long? [_]{2*$PQ}

*Note:* For the vector answers use < >, for example <0,0,0>.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a) [`` PQ = [$Q]-[$P] = [$PQ]``]

b) The length is [``|\vec{v}| = \sqrt{([$PQ->{data}[0]])^2 + ([$PQ->{data}[1]])^2 + ([$PQ->{data}[2]])^2 } = [$norm]``]

c) The tip is at [``[$X]+[$PQ] = [$X+$PQ]``]

d) The tail would be at [``[$Y]-[$PQ] = [$Y-$PQ]``]

e) This is found as [`` -1 \cdot [$PQ] = [$PQ*-1]``].

f) This is found as [`` 2 \cdot [$PQ] = [$PQ*2]``].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
